# Morning Aroma — Environment Variables (ORIGINAL hypothetical plan — see note below)
#
# This prototype's frontend runs entirely in-memory and needs NONE of these to work —
# `npm install && npm run dev` is genuinely all it takes.
#
# IMPORTANT: this file documents the *original* broad hypothetical plan (Next.js API routes +
# Redis + NextAuth + a headless CMS). That's not what actually got built. The real backend that
# exists and is deployed lives in `server/` and is simpler than this — a standalone Express API
# (not Next.js routes), custom JWT auth (not NextAuth.js), no Redis. See `server/.env.example` for
# what that real, deployed backend actually needs — that file is the accurate one to follow.
# This file is kept as a record of the original broader plan for whichever of these pieces
# (CMS, media storage, the rest of the data model) still get built later, per `ROADMAP.md`.

# --- Database (PostgreSQL, e.g. via Prisma — see prisma/schema.prisma) ---
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/morning_aroma"

# --- Redis (OTP codes, session cache, recommendation cache) ---
REDIS_URL="redis://localhost:6379"

# --- NextAuth.js ---
NEXTAUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"
NEXTAUTH_SECRET="generate-a-long-random-string-here"

# --- Google OAuth (for "Continue with Google") ---
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=""
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=""

# --- Email (for OTP delivery) ---
EMAIL_SERVER_HOST="smtp.example.com"
EMAIL_SERVER_PORT="587"
EMAIL_SERVER_USER=""
EMAIL_SERVER_PASSWORD=""
EMAIL_FROM="Morning Aroma <no-reply@morningaroma.com>"

# --- Paystack (checkout / payments — per the project owner's decision) ---
PAYSTACK_PUBLIC_KEY=""
PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY=""

# --- CMS (Strapi or Sanity — pick one, per the original brief) ---
CMS_API_URL=""
CMS_API_TOKEN=""

# --- Media storage (Cloudinary or S3/CloudFront) ---
CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=""
CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=""
CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=""
# — or —
AWS_S3_BUCKET=""
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=""
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=""
AWS_REGION=""

# --- App-level ---
NODE_ENV="development"
